  "summary_en": "European Commission Communication endorsing seven key requirements for trustworthy, human-centric AI drawn from the High-Level Expert Group's ethics guidelines. It launches a stakeholder piloting phase of the assessment list, outlines international cooperation, and announces related work on safety and liability frameworks. Non-binding.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Endorses seven key requirements for trustworthy AI (human agency and oversight, robustness, privacy and data governance, transparency, fairness, societal well-being, accountability).",
   "Guidelines are non-binding and create no new legal obligations.",
   "Launches piloting phase from June 2019 to test the assessment list, with review in early 2020.",
   "Commits to promote international consensus on human-centric AI with partners and in G7/G20.",
   "Announces a report on AI safety and liability frameworks and Product Liability Directive guidance."
  ],
